

Looking across `cylon-command.js`, `cylon-dos.js`, `qandyland.js`, and `qandyland-univac.js`, the two systems share the same filesystem concepts (`_dir.sys!`, `qandy-ramdrive` v2 JSON, `<dir>` tokens, `X`-prefixed TTL timestamps), so bringing them closer together is very natural.

---

### 1. Adding `save`, `copy`, and `<c>` Clipboard to `qandyland.js`

#### `save` and `copy`
`qandyland.js` already has `fileSave(driveName, cwd, name, content, session, owner)` internally—it just isn't wired into the console `switch (cmd)` block.
* **`save <file> <text>`**: Wire directly to `fileSave(_serverMountedDrive, _serverCwd, target, text, 'console', 'console')`.
* **`copy <src> <dst>`**: Currently `qandyland.js` only has `rename`. Adding `copy` (reading via `fileLoad` and writing via `fileSave`) also gives you a clean place to attach `<c>`.

#### How `<c>` works in Node (`qandyland.js`)
`cylon-command.js` uses `navigator.clipboard`, which only exists in the browser. In `qandyland.js`, `<c>` can shell out synchronously with `child_process.execFileSync` / `spawnSync` based on `process.platform`:
* **Windows (`win32`)**: write via `clip`, read via `powershell -NoProfile -Command Get-Clipboard`
* **macOS (`darwin`)**: `pbcopy` / `pbpaste`
* **Linux (`linux`)**: `wl-copy` / `wl-paste` (Wayland) or `xclip -selection clipboard` / `xsel -b` (X11)
* **Headless/cloud (e.g., Render)**: wrap in `try/catch` and return a clear error (`Clipboard unavailable in headless environment`) so `<c>` works locally for DevTeam without crashing remote deployments.

#### Two small REPL cleanups you'll want while touching `qandyland.js`:
1. **`return;` vs `break;` bug**: In `qandyland.js`'s `rl.on('line')` `switch (cmd)`, many cases (`export`, `import`, `mount`, `unmount`, `dir`, `ls`, `mkdir`, `cd`, `rmdir`, `rename`, `exam`, `type`, `delete`) use `return;` instead of `break;`, which skips `rl.prompt()` at the end of the handler.
2. **Flush debounced `_dir.sys!` on exit**: `fileSave` uses `_debounceSaveManifestToStorage` (50ms timer). If you run `save` then `exit` quickly (or programmatically save right before shutdown), flush any pending `_manifestDebounceTimers` inside the `exit`/`shutdown` handler before closing.
3. **Argument parsing**: `parseQuotedArgs` in `qandyland.js` only handles double quotes and joins `arg` back into a single space-delimited string. Switching to `cylon-command.js`'s `parseArgs` (which supports `'...'`, `"..."`, and `\"` escapes) makes `save <file> <text>` and `copy <src> <dst>` work cleanly.

