### 2. Cross-Pollination: Cylon DOS $\leftrightarrow$ `qandyland.js`

#### What `qandyland.js` would benefit from in `cylon-dos.js` / `cylon-command.js`
* **`alpha [dir]`**: In `cylon-command.js`, `alpha` dumps every variable file in `/a/` (or any directory) as `name = value`. In `qandyland.js`, checking `a/gfxSpawn`, `a/gfxZBase`, `a/gfxOdometer`, etc. currently requires `ls` + multiple `type` commands.
* **Wildcards in `dir`, `ls`, and `delete`**: `qandyland.js` already has `matchPattern()` and `fileSearch()`, and `dirList()` even accepts a `pattern` parameter, but the console `dir`, `ls`, and `delete` cases don't pass wildcard arguments to them. `cylon-dos.js`'s `extractWildcard()` pattern lets `delete w/Bc/Va*` or `dir *.gfx` work uniformly.
* **Drive-prefixed paths (`drive:/path`) and `drive:` switching**: `cylon-dos.js`'s `ref()` allows cross-drive `copy` (e.g. `copy cylon-queville.gfx:/q/log cylon-capflag.gfx:/q/log`) and keeps per-drive `cwd`, instead of having a single `_serverMountedDrive`.
* **`importDrive` replace vs. merge mode**: In `cylon-dos.js`, `importDrive` supports both replacing a drive cleanly and merging (`mode: 'merge'`). In `qandyland.js`, `importDrive` only merges, leaving deleted entries behind if re-importing over an existing drive.
* **Clean `X`-timestamp GC everywhere**: `qandyland.js` only expires `X`-prefixed files inside `fileList()`. If `fileLoad()` or `dirList()` hits an expired entry before `fileList()` runs, it will still return it. Checking `X` expiration inside `fileLoad` and `dirList` (or running a light sweep) matches `cylon-dos.js` behavior.






